  <h1>SMT: Training RNNs Without Ever Unrolling Them</h1>
  <p class="lead">Backpropagation through time suffers from O(T) gradient paths that vanish or explode — BPTT is sequential, unstable, and fundamentally limits nonlinear RNNs. Supervised Memory Training sidesteps recurrent credit propagation entirely by asking a different question: what if a Transformer told the RNN exactly what it should remember at each step? The result is O(1) gradient paths, time-parallel training, and nonlinear RNNs that actually capture long-range dependencies.</p>
