<section id="s-method" data-code="method">
<div class="section-no">03 — SMT Architecture</div>
<h2>Decoupling representation from dynamics</h2>

<p>SMT has three components trained jointly: an <strong>encoder E</strong> (bidirectional Transformer), a <strong>decoder D</strong> (causal Transformer), and the <strong>RNN f</strong> (the model you actually want).</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Encoder E:</strong> Takes the full past context [x0...xt] and produces memory label mt. Because it's bidirectional and only needs past tokens, it can run in parallel over all timesteps.</li>
  <li><strong>Decoder D:</strong> Given memory mt, predicts future outputs [yt...y_T]. This is the future-prediction objective that forces mt to be a predictive state.</li>
  <li><strong>RNN f:</strong> Learns the one-step transition (mt, xt₊1) → mt₊1 using the encoder labels as ground truth. Never unrolled during training.</li>
</ul>

