<p>The three training losses work together:</p>

<div class="math-block">
  <div class="math-label">SMT Training Objective</div>
  <span class="math-var">L_smt</span> = λ_dec · <span class="math-var">L_dec</span> + λ_dyn · <span class="math-var">L_dyn</span> + λ_unif · <span class="math-var">L_unif</span><br>
  <br>
  <span class="math-var">L_dec</span> = CE(y_future, D(mt, x_future)) &nbsp; <span class="math-comment">— encoder learns predictive states</span><br>
  <span class="math-var">L_dyn</span> = MSE(f(mt, xt₊1), mt₊1) &nbsp; <span class="math-comment">— RNN learns one-step update</span><br>
  <span class="math-var">L_unif</span> = log E[exp(-2‖ma - m_b‖²)] &nbsp; <span class="math-comment">— prevent memory collapse</span>
</div>

<p>The key property: the longest gradient path in SMT is <em>O(1)</em>. The encoder reads the past context in parallel. The RNN's dynamics loss is purely one-step — no unrolling, no chain of Jacobians, no vanishing or exploding.</p>

