<p>This memory visualization reveals that SMT does not just learn to compress randomly — it learns <em>task-appropriate</em> compression. The predictive state objective acts as an information bottleneck: squeeze out everything the future doesn't need.</p>

<p>Crucially, the RNN's transition function then only needs to implement simple transitions between these few memory states — far easier than learning the full combinatorial dynamics BPTT would require. The Transformer encoder does the hard representational work; the RNN handles the sequential updates.</p>
</section>


