<h3>Sequential compute efficiency</h3>
<p>SMT trains significantly more efficiently in sequential compute (FLOPs on an infinitely parallel machine — the true bottleneck on modern hardware). For the Transformer-backbone RNN on TinyStories, SMT needs ~10× fewer sequential FLOPs to reach the same loss as BPTT. The result is even stronger on pixel modeling, where long-range credit assignment is essential.</p>

